Riot Games' root certificate for the League of Legends game client API (the Live Client Data API that the
game serves on https://127.0.0.1:2999 while a match runs). Prism Deck's LoL poller (gamelink-lol-client.js)
trusts this certificate and nothing else for that one connection.

Source (downloaded unchanged on 2026-10-17):
  https://static.developer.riotgames.com/docs/lol/riotgames.pem
Riot's docs name it as the root to validate the game client's self-signed certificate with:
  https://developer.riotgames.com/docs/lol#game-client-api_root-certificatessl-errors

Subject = Issuer: C=US, ST=California, L=Santa Monica, O=Riot Games, OU=LoL Game Engineering,
  CN=LoL Game Engineering Certificate Authority, emailAddress=gametechnologies@riotgames.com
X.509 v1 (no extensions), RSA 2048, sha1WithRSAEncryption, valid 2013-12-04 to 2043-11-27
SHA-256 fingerprint: CA:8C:9D:32:5B:4C:DC:46:4C:6C:94:A5:85:C8:5E:91:EC:23:D4:0B:A5:BF:3A:E2:82:2B:95:1A:4A:50:4E:A3
(the poller refuses to start if the certificate below does not have exactly this fingerprint)

